<title>UK: BAA first-half pretax profit up 3.4 percent.</title>
<headline>BAA first-half pretax profit up 3.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to Sept 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		 22.2		  vs  21.5</p>
<p> Dividend (pence)	   4.5		  vs   4.125</p>
<p> Pretax		     304		    vs 294</p>
<p> Turnover		   742		    vs 698</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts for pre-tax profits were in a range of 303 to 320 million stg, and for a dividend of 4.6 pence.  </p>
<p> Operating result	 323		    vs 304</p>
<p> Exceptional gains	nil		    vs   9</p>
<p> Interest		    18		    vs  18</p>
<p> Tax			   74		    vs  72</p>
<p> Net taxed		  230		    vs 222</p>
<p> Attributable	     183		    vs 179</p>
<p> Pay date		   Jan 21 1997</p>
<p>Div registration date  Nov 26 1996  </p>
<p>NOTE - BAA said as a result of seasonal fluctuations in airport charges, income from landing and passenger handling fees was reduced in the first half by 11 milion stg from a year ago. But it said this would be recoverable in the second half of the year.</p>
<p>The company said first-half results last year included a 9.0 million stg exceptional gain on a property sale.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
